Oct 22

Tuesday
Today was DCM, and afterwards a lovely exchange With Elder Wilson. Fun
fact, it was actually his Last exchange, and my first =F0=9F=98=82 He gave =
me a lot
of good advice about missionary work in general; we used a few different
ways to reach out to people. We first did just a little streeting, then
after went to a nearby station and did some sign streeting. Usually it
doesn't go well from my experience, but like 10 seconds after I held up the
sign, a lady walked right over to us, and is gonna bring her boyfriend to
Eikaiwa in Okamachi (the area that Elder Wilson is from). Was a huge
miracle! Later that night we also probably deposited around 100-150 flyers
into people's mailboxes lol. Was very fun =F0=9F=98=81 we also had our tran=
sfer
video, which didn't change much besides Ishizaka=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 transfer=
ring to Akashi,
which is sad =F0=9F=98=A2 But it'll be ok, we get Kyoumen=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81=
 in his place; he's a riot.

Wednesday
Today before Eikaiwa, a dude named Sanchew came to the church to make music
with Sonomura=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, as I drew on the sidelines lol. He was sup=
er nice, and his
voice is extremely high =F0=9F=98=82 he brought a guitar and was singing up=
 a storm.
He actually stayed at the chyrch building for like 5 hours probably lol. We
had Eikaiwa with him, and afterwards he even stayed for a decent while
during Badminton. Was awesome! In Eikaiwa we talked almost only about food;
Elder Berg has the advanced class structured basically as a big
conversation, so we basically just talked about random foods in English for
an hour lol.

Thursday
Today we were planning to go to a festival for a bunch of the morning, but
when we got there, oddly nobody was there. Turns out Sonomura=E9=95=B7=E8=
=80=81 had the
wrong month =F0=9F=98=82 Anyways, I spent a lot of the day with Ishizaka=E9=
=95=B7=E8=80=81, as he
needed to impart his final wisdom to Mr before he transferred. I asked if I
could call a bunch of inactive members numbers, and he taught me a bit,
then let me do the rest =F0=9F=98=81 It was a bit nerve-racking but great p=
ractice!
We also did a lot of travel, getting from Ibaraki to Hirakata is an hour
nomatter how you get there lol. When we got back to Ibaraki, Ishizaka=E9=95=
=B7=E8=80=81 and
I taught a lesson to Mahinda=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F, a new member in our ward. H=
e's maybe the
nicest dude I=E2=80=99ve met. There are low-key a lot of people I want to s=
ay that
about, but it=E2=80=99s still true =F0=9F=98=82 Later that night we had Bas=
ketball as usual,
and I was able to share some of my art while others played basketball;
still fun. Afterwards, we taught a lesson, idk what it was about or who it
was with, but I had it written down so I'm pretty sure it happened =F0=9F=
=98=82 I
could just check the =E2=80=9CArea Book=E2=80=9D but I've gotta write, so f=
or now just
pretend it was a super touching story =F0=9F=91=8D=F0=9F=91=8D

Friday
We met with Mahinda=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F again, and this time he bought us all=
 donuts, again
super nice dude. Later we ate again at the Fukudas, This time it was
okonomiaki, but I was actually so close to throwing up from how much I ate.
They would not stop making food =F0=9F=92=80 Later I somehow was feeling ok=
, and we
met again with Rui. He's again super nice, and feels like an American
friend, but hes just gotta get to more church and activities, He's still a
member but just thinks the other church members here are weird =F0=9F=98=82=
 We will
fix this =F0=9F=91=8D=F0=9F=91=8D=F0=9F=91=8D =F0=9F=98=82 Anyways, he also=
 told us he works for JT, which is
apparently Japan Tobacco or something =F0=9F=98=82 he says he doesnt tell h=
is boss
about his beliefs or anything or he'd probably get fired lol. He still
works there because it pays well lol. That night at the Gathering Place, I
pretty much taught Nao a lesson all by myself while everyone else taught a
big lesson a few chairs away from us lol. Shes not a member, but says she
wants to be a senior missionary in Utah =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 love the p=
assion, let's just
move forward then lol. After we git home, we played our last game of Catan
with Ishizaka=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81, pretty sure Berg=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 won =F0=
=9F=98=A2

Saturday
Today we got some more Indo Curry with President Sano=E2=80=99s son. I got =
the
spicest that they had, and it was perfectly fine lol. I gotta find some
real spicy stuff someday =F0=9F=98=82 We had a fun meeting at the church fo=
r our
=E2=80=9Cward conference eve=E2=80=9D. Later we git to visit Moriguchi san=
=E2=80=99s apartment, her
kids are the cutest ever =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=827

Sunday

Church taught primary for about 5 mins,
afterwards had lunch with moriguchi and toyama San. Toyama only made it to
the luncheon part, but it was awesome; he got to talk a bunch with the
members! Also got to say hi to Yu=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F again, this time he tol=
d me he
specifically wants to be a captain in Germany So he can pilot a german made
ship. Love this guy.

Pday
Today we went Shopping for most of the day lol. First we went to a
cards/game shop, which was very neat, also kind of crazy how cheap some old
games were (and how expensive some others were lol). We tried to visit a
cool big statue bit it was unfortunately closed =F0=9F=98=95 was still fun =
to bike
there though! Near the place of the statue there was a massive mall, so we
went and looked around, was very fun. Not a bunch else to say unfortunately
lol.

Sorry some stuff isn't super detailed, I'm typing like a menace ATM =F0=9F=
=98=82 Love
you guys!!!
I mean it!! I will try to get back to yall next Pday, sorry =F0=9F=98=85
Bye!
-=E3=82=AD=E3=83=AA=E3=82=A2=E3=83=B3=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81

Today's spiritual message is simple; think of something/someone you are
grateful for, and think about why you are grateful for it/them. Pray about
it, and let God know you are appreciative, and I promise that you will be
able to feel that he hears that. It's true :)
Bye!

--000000000000a8b7a4062589f29a
